# VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client examples.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@key = dev-key

### Create two accounts
# @name alice
POST {{host}}/v1/accounts
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: create-alice-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"owner": "alice", "currency": "USD"}

###
# @name bob
POST {{host}}/v1/accounts
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: create-bob-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"owner": "bob", "currency": "USD"}

### Fund alice (treasury -> alice)
POST {{host}}/v1/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/deposits
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: deposit-alice-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": 10000, "reference": "card settlement #881"}

### Transfer alice -> bob. Re-send this exact request: you get the same
### 201 body back with Idempotent-Replay: true and no second debit.
POST {{host}}/v1/transfers
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: order-42
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "to_account_id": "{{bob.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": 2500,
  "currency": "USD",
  "reference": "order 42"
}

### Same key, different payload -> 422
POST {{host}}/v1/transfers
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: order-42
Content-Type: application/json

{"from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.id}}", "to_account_id": "{{bob.response.body.id}}", "amount": 1, "currency": "USD"}

### Statement with keyset pagination
GET {{host}}/v1/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/entries?limit=2
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Metrics
GET {{host}}/metrics
